  "releaseNotes": "Adds a net11.0 build, for .NET 11. The netstandard2.0, net8.0, net9.0 and net10.0 builds stay, so nothing changes for a project on an earlier .NET. The major version is 11 because it follows the .NET generation, as 10.0.0 did for .NET 10: no API was added, changed or removed since 10.1.0.15, and code that builds against 10.1.0.15 builds against 11.0.0 as it is. On .NET Standard 2.0 only (which is what .NET Framework uses), the System.Text.Json and Microsoft.Bcl.AsyncInterfaces dependencies move from 10.0.13 to 11.0.0. On .NET 8 and later the package still has no dependencies.",
